tg wrote:
> What do you generally do - make a wish right away or use it as a
> permanent light source?

If your character has yet to acquire DSM from another source, it's
really not a hard choice to make, either gray or silver dragon scale
mail is better than any other choice unless the player is in a special
situation, one that demands a specific item.  The AC bonus is too great
to ignore, plus the opportunity to get a major intrinsic out of the way
to boot, AND it doesn't add an artifact to the game.

Sometimes I wonder what Nethack would be like without DSM, or at least
with it knocked down a few AC points so it wasn't the absolute best
armor in the game.  I wonder if the game would be improved as a result.
 Sometimes I even suspect it would.  Ah well.

There may be specific quest artifacts that might be a better wish in
some cases; half physical damage could be useful in the very early game
even with a bad AC, if magic resistance is already available.  However
many players choose not to wish for those things.

